<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 238 0 R/E(The "Youth to Business" project was a 3-month initiative by AIESEC in Rwanda, endorsed by The Commonwealth Year of Youth, aimed at fostering innovation and entrepreneurship among Rwandan youth. It involved three phases: soliciting business ideas, providing incubation and training, and awarding the best ideas in collaboration with industry experts. The project aimed to equip youths with the skills and support to turn their ideas into successful businesses, thus contributing to Rwanda's economic growth.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[2]>>
